incident :the_sanchakou_ring do
  name "The Sanchakou Ring"
  tags :ecology, :catastrophe, :prediction, :agriculture
  prominence :marginal

  prose <<~PROSE
    Compartment Twelve of the current register at #{ref :tangwang_post, "Tangwang Post"}: two hectares of larch and birch on the Tangwang's east bank, with four apple-pear rows and a hazel coppice at its south corner belonging to #{ref :sanchakou, "Sanchakou"}. #{ref :continuity, "Continuity"}'s deviation cabinet opened the file on 14 September 2089, on the ninth consecutive reading above the reach's threshold.

    Two of #{ref :xie_lanting, "Xie Lanting"}'s twenty cores contained closed sleeves of foreign tissue, below the reach threshold of four, in September and again at bud-break. #{ref :nadya_tsoi, "Nadya Tsoi"} walked the compartment on the thirtieth of May in #{year :now} CE and marked it two days later. The ring closed on the twelfth of June: 2,914 stems, nine crew, one hammer, between 04:12 and 20:40.
  PROSE

  prose <<~PROSE, section: :course, heading: "Between The Mark And The Cut"
    Publication of the new band under #{ref :the_ring_order, "the ring order"} put Sanchakou 1,600 metres inside it. The settlement's thirty-one households moved south along the same road in the eleven days between the mark and the ring, carrying the charter name, the clinic team, the work rota and the grave register. #{ref :the_great_root, "The Great Root"} entered the move as a completed transfer with no household separated and no service interrupted.

    Two of the compartment's corner witnesses stood inside the ring line. Post surveyors moved those corners outward on the eleventh, blazed and entered three new trees at each, and the hammer left the peg the following morning.

    The crew worked the north edge inward. Every stem over 40 millimetres took a ring at 1.3 metres, packed with lime-and-oil paste and struck with the number above the cut; smaller stems were cut at the collar and the faces painted. The number is what will separate these stems from the ones #{ref :the_others, "the Others"} kill in the same ground. The tally closed at 2,914 against the hammer count and the crew came out through the apple-pear rows at the south corner.
  PROSE

  prose <<~PROSE, section: :aftermath, heading: "Sixty Sticks"
    Xie had cut the orchard's scionwood in March, dormant, before the file was anywhere near a mark: sixty sticks off the four rows, grafted onto rootstock in the post's nursery bed in April and carried to the new row's ground with the households. The cabinet filed on the cutting and again on the release. Tsoi allowed both.

    Sanchakou's petition to lift the graves off the burial rise was refused, because soil does not cross outward from a band under an open file. The rise stands two hundred and fifty metres behind the ring line, inside the band, and is entered four times a year on the coring team's round.

    Forty-three of the sixty grafts were in leaf by the second week after the move. The cabinet enters the count each week and has not closed the input.
  PROSE
end
